# BACKLOG — Ideas, deferred features, priorities

> **Purpose (L2):** a **living** list of pending things — with priority and a
> reason (usually "deferred, see §X of FEATURES for context"). Written from Phase 1
> (first idea) and extended. Planned 📋 features in `FEATURES.md` must be resolvable
> to a backlog entry — not duplicate prose.

## 1. Core / next in line (P1)
- [ ] <feature> — why it matters, acceptance hint, blocks future work.
- [ ] <chore> — infra/quality, estimates.

## 2. Deferred backend / server-side (P2/P3)
- [ ] <feature> — deferred because: ⏳ #<reason/priority>.

## 3. UI / frontend (L3·frontend-app P1)
- [ ] <screen> — what the user does, which module it touches.

## 4. Quality / infra (P2)
- [ ] E2E coverage for <scenario>
- [ ] docker image build in CI (prevent §2.3 regression-silent)

## 5. Ideas (P3 / do later)
- [ ] <idea> — one-liner of the value.

## Summary (top counts)
> Let's keep the header counters honest: `P1: a · P2: b · P3: c`.

---
> **Rule:** every properly-specified task on deck has: a goal, acceptance criteria, a
> priority, and a reference to the doc it belongs to (FEATURES/REVIEW). The backlog is
> "> delivery BEFORE specs have buy-in — not promises.